WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I want to
talk about another thing

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.336
that happened this year --
recently, about a month ago,

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.772
where I thought you might be too
jittery, but you kept your cool.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
We went and saw
Bruce Springsteen on Broadway.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.409
-Bruce Springsteen, "The Boss."
-Yeah.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The best. The best.
-It was a birthday present.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:13.847 line:92%
-It was a birthday present.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.815
-And then, afterwards, we got to
say hi to Bruce Springsteen.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.518
-And I don't know why I thought
that that wouldn't happen,

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I didn't think
it would happen.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you're supposed to not
think it's gonna happen.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.423 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a surprise.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.090 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-But, sometimes --

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.393 size:81% position:41%
-That's where she's at
in her life right now.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:27.827 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-If she didn't meet him,

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
it might have been
like, "Oh, bummer."

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:30.196 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you did
and you took a picture.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, Dad, I have a question,
'cause I'm gonna show

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
the picture of
Mom and Bruce Springsteen.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:39.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has Mom ever
looked that happy with you?

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:46.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can I hold that up a second?
-Yeah, yeah. Sure.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.281 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I got to look closer.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
No.
-Yeah.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I have to say,
it was really nice,

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.753 size:78% position:39%
'cause I wasn't gonna
ask for a picture,

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you were not gonna
ask for a picture.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we said hello
and we were walking out,

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:00.226
and his beautiful, talented
wife, Patti Scialfa, said,

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.562
"Bruce, you have to take
a picture with Seth's mom."

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:03.063 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.798 size:88% position:44%
-And then you repaid her
by getting real handsy

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:07.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Bruce Springsteen
right here.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there's
another picture, though,

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he's
actually smooching me.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:11.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.872 line:92%
-I don't know if I saw that one.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:18.645
-At your wedding, you guys --
for the, like, mother-son dance,

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.380 line:92%
sang, like, an unusual song.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first dance --
Well, not our first dance.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"She's the --"
-No, "For You."

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"For You."
"I came for you."

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.253 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Yeah. And it was nice.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's not a very common
first-dance song.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. It was like
a jitterbug dance,

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.192 line:92%
and people didn't expect that.

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.927 line:92%
-No. Well, there was a lot that

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:38.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
they didn't
expect from our wedding.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, another thing
I want to say --

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.734 line:92%
we showed a video of Ashe,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, a couple years ago
on this show,

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
we announced that
we were having Ashe.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.707 size:84% position:42%
And, so, I want to take
this opportunity now --

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:48.374 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You guys obviously know.

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:51.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
But my wife and I are
expecting a second baby.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.481 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:59.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
And...very excited.
Thank you. Very excited.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:04.023 size:78% position:39%
-So, I have to say --
I get the phone call,

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:07.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my Seth
is sometimes a crier.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.195 line:92%
-Yeah. Quite a bit, quite a bit.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:12.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. So, he's
crying on the phone

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.567 line:92%
and he can't catch his breath.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.235 size:75% position:38% line:92%
He's, like, sobbing.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "What?
What happened? Are you okay?"

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.872 size:78% position:39%
And he said, "No, no.
It's wonderful news.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.640 size:78% position:39%
It's wonderful news."
I said, "What is it?"

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.976
And he said, "Well,
we're gonna have another baby."

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "That's fabulous.
Why are you crying?"

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said,
"Because, for over a month,

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:31.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've had to pretend that
I don't care what sex it is,

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:31.818 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and I do care.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:37.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want a little boy
so we can be Sufi and Posh.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's true.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really wanted
a brother for my son

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I was
so lucky to have one.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. They've always been
the best of friends.

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:45.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two years apart,
and that's exactly what

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ashe and Albert
are gonna be, right?

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, now, okay, so, you...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause we have not
decided on a name.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:57.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, Dad, explain why you
feel so strongly about Albert.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:02.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, for the old sweats that
have been here every year,

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:06.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've had five sheepdogs,
and they're all named Albert.

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:07.887 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We have Albert V.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:10.890 line:92%
And I really love the dog.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.493 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I always wonder

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:16.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
what it would sound like
if it could talk.

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:22.101
But I never hear, like, a voice,
like, on a cartoon or a movie

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
or a child that, "That's what
Albert would sound like."

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:31.110
So I figure if they name
the kid Albert, eventually,

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:36.049
he'll start to talk, and
I'll say, "Oh, yeah, that's it."

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:40.153
And this is a
little bit sad on Thanksgiving,

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:43.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the kid's gonna
outlive the dog.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:43.923 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:48.261 size:81% position:41%
-And so if I have a --
It's like Pinocchio.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.495 line:92%
You know, he becomes a real --

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:54.000
The dog becomes a real boy,
and everything works out.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's great.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
You know my wife.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think this
would be a tough sell?

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.841 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, no. Wait.
We have one advantage.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:08.181
She is big on the A's, so I know
it's gonna be an "A" name.

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:08.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Right.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can I tell you
that the fact it's been

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:13.653
five of our dogs's names
has eliminated it from --

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can tell us that,
but it doesn't mean

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:16.923 line:92%
we have to stop hoping for it.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:17.490 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's true.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, by the way,
I have another son.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:22.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who knows, someday,
if that doesn't work out?

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:23.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hypothetically,
if you had a child,

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:26.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
would Albert be eliminated
as a possibility?

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:29.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Albert was my name in
her French class.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:30.470 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I think it's a great name.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:32.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
-It is a great name.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:33.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
-All right.

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:37.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hillary's voting for Bruce,
by the way.

